  :seon.turn/reply
  "I've been thrashing. Let me settle down and actually read the two functions I was told to read.\n\nThe proof I already have from `source-fn`:\n\n**`reply-map`** joins entries with `\", \"`, but when a previous entry's text *ends in a comment* (like an elided value's trailing `;; …N = N more …` legend) it emits a `\"\\n \"` instead, and adds a trailing `\"\\n\"` before `}` when the last entry ends in a comment. So the splice of shown text into the map is what breaks EDN — the value's own text is dropped in verbatim, comments and all.\n\n**`value-text`** just returns the saved shown text unchanged.\n\n**`response-entries`** puts `:seon.repl/value` (and `:error`, `:findings`, `:diagnostics`) as the *present keys* already text — but crucially flattens them via `reply-map`, so a rendered value keeps `:value` only, while an elided value's `;;` legend corrupts the map.\n\nLet me look at the elision/finding side and the test to understand what \"reads back as EDN\" requires.\n\n```clojure\n(clojure.repl/source-fn 'seon.repl/ends-in-comment?)\n```\n\nLet me also see the proof test's expectations:\n\n```clojure\n(clojure.repl/source-fn 'seon.repl-test/the-reply-is-one-edn-map-whatever-the-value)\n```\n\nI need both before I write anything.\n\n```clojure\n[(clojure.repl/source-fn 'seon.repl/ends-in-comment?)\n (clojure.repl/source-fn 'seon.repl-test/the-reply-is-one-edn-map-whatever-the-value)\n (clojure.repl/source-fn 'seon.repl/findings)]\n```",
