the map (not quoted), because `one-map` reads the whole map and the value position inside it should read as that vector.\n\nSo the value key for an elided value should be the raw text if it reads as EDN, else the data it decodes to. Let me write `value-text` to return the shown text unchanged (as-is), but have `response-entries` splices it so the map reads back. For the comment case `\"[1 2]\\n;; a trailing diagnostic line\"`, the value key must be `[1 2]` — i.e. the comment must be stripped.\n\nGiven limited turns, the cleanest fix: in `response-entries`, set the `:seon.repl/value` to `(or (read-shown value tagged-literal) value)` wrapped so it prints as EDN, and for comment-ended text, strip trailing comment lines first. Let me write it and run the test.\n\n```clojure\n(defn- reply-map\n  {:malli/schema [:=> [:cat [:vector [:tuple :qualified-keyword :string]]] [:maybe :string]]}\n  [entries]\n  (when (seq entries)\n    (str \"",
